<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Lesser Nogai Horde</h1><p class="st-meta">1557 CE – 1637 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The western branch of the Nogai Horde, which moved to the Kuban steppe and became a client of the Crimean Khanate and the Ottomans.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1557, amid a civil war within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nogai-horde">Nogai Horde</a> over relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the mirza Kazy broke away with his followers and moved west across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> to the steppes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> and the Kuban. The new group became known as Kazy's Ulus or the Lesser Nogai Horde.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nogais">Nogais</a> were pastoral nomads who raided Muscovite and Caucasian lands, often in alliance with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crimean-khanate">Crimean Khanate</a>. They were ruled by mirzas of Kazy's line and recognised Crimean and, through it, Ottoman overlordship. Their horses and captives were traded through the Crimean ports.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the early 17th century many Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nogais">Nogais</a> moved closer to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crimean-khanate">Crimean Khanate</a>, especially after <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kalmyk-khanate">Kalmyk Khanate</a> pressure in the 1630s. They were absorbed into the Crimean and Kuban Nogai communities, which were later annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1783.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lesser-nogai-horde.jpg" alt="Lesser Nogai Horde" width="320" height="227"><figcaption>Image: Devlet Geray · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BlackSea1600_ru.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1557 CE – 1637 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kazy Mirza</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Nogai</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kazy's Ulus, Little Nogai Horde</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1597&amp;focus=lesser-nogai-horde" aria-label="Lesser Nogai Horde on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5639 196 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lesser Nogai Horde lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6209 768h0M5808 852h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5959 452h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5959 452h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Russia. <a href="/atlas?year=1597&amp;focus=lesser-nogai-horde">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
